WorkRoles replaces the Work tab with role-based work management. No setup required, safe to remove if you don't like it.

Instead of assigning priority numbers, you assign a set of ordered roles to colonists. A role is simply a named set of ordered jobs. Priorities are calculated and set automatically behind the scenes.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mnmr/rw.eprime/main/WorkRoles/images/feature-drag-drop.png[/img]

Set up a role once and hand it to any number of colonists. You can then adjust everyone by toggling or editing the role.

[h1]Key Features[/h1]
[list]
[*][b]No Priorities:[/b] Roles are just ordered lists of jobs (whole work types like Cooking or single jobs like Smelting). Assignments are processed left-to-right, so earlier roles win (and within a role, earlier jobs win).
[*][b]No Setup:[/b] Seeds pre-made roles covering every vanilla and official DLC work type. Auto-assigns roles to match existing priorities.
[*][b]Easy Switching:[/b] Toggle any role globally or per colonist, without touching the underlying assignments. No more remembering what priorities colonists used to have.
[*][b]Overlapping Roles:[/b] The same job can live in multiple roles, and a colonist can hold both. Assign [i]Emergency Harvester[/i] at high priority but disabled, and when blight or a cold snap hits, one click to enable the role sends everyone to the fields.
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mnmr/rw.eprime/main/WorkRoles/images/feature-toggles.png[/img]
[*][b]Rules Engine:[/b] Configure roles to only be enabled at certain times of day or at specific locations (settlements, the gravship, caravans).
[*][b]Bill Support:[/b] Restrict work bills to a particular role. Especially useful when a bill requires multiple skills.
[*][b]Deep Job Control:[/b] The role editor provides a filterable job tree. Jobs within a role can be freely reordered. All of the seeded roles can be edited or removed.
[*][b]Suitability Insights:[/b] Role chips show a suitability verdict for the selected colonist.
[*][b]Smart Recommendations:[/b] A per-colonist panel suggests roles from burning passions, gene aptitudes, colony-best skills, training opportunities and colony needs. 
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mnmr/rw.eprime/main/WorkRoles/images/feature-advisor.png[/img]
[*][b]Import/Export:[/b] Easily share or backup your role setup.
[*][b]Performance:[/b] Extensive caching, rendering from pre-calculated caches, scoped invalidation, no per-tick logic.
[*][b]Automation:[/b] You can enable automation in Options to have WorkRoles automatically manage role assignments for you.
[*][b]Modded Jobs:[/b] Jobs added by mods are mostly unassigned by default; the role editor warns when a job isn't in any role.
[/list]

[h1]Role Types[/h1]
An initial role set is seeded into the game, covering all detected work types and jobs.
[list]
[*][b]Combo Roles:[/b] Various roles (Basics, Farmer, Grunt) that combine multiple work types to make work assignment easier.
[*][b]Composite Roles:[/b] Compose new roles from other roles to re-use your existing definitions.
[*][b]Conditional Roles:[/b] Specify rules that govern at what times and/or location a role should be enabled.
[*][b]Blocker Roles:[/b] Used to prevent work from any subsequent role assignment.
[*][b]Extra Roles:[/b] Training roles that enable role progression and convenience roles to make prioritization easier.
[/list]

[h1]Recommendation Logic[/h1]
[list]
[*][b]Colony Needs:[/b] Keeps essential roles covered; configurable per role via recommendation tuning options.
[*][b]Suggestions:[/b] Uses passions, genes, traits, skills/expertise and training paths; armed workers also get skill-tiered Hunting recommendations.
[*][b]Applying:[/b] Cherry-pick for one colonist or preview and apply colony-wide. Pin assignments that must stay untouched.
[*][b]Protected:[/b] Conditional roles, pinned roles and blockers are never suggested, moved or removed.
[*][b]Genetics:[/b] Those afraid of fire get Pyrophobe before Core.
[*][b]Signal Visibility:[/b] Skill tooltips show every signal behind a recommendation verdict.
[/list]

[h1]How It Works[/h1]
[list]
[*]Role assignments are translated into an ordered list of jobs. Duplicate jobs are trimmed from the list (only the earliest job is kept; jobs in disabled roles are skipped), before it is handed to the game (which is also what the vanilla priority grid does). 
[*]Emergency jobs (firefighting, urgent tending, going to bed for emergency treatment) interrupt everything (by default, only when in any of the first five enabled role assignments, with an option to always allow interruptions).
[*]Other mods that read priorities get the values WorkRoles computed. Setting priorities is owned by WorkRoles (which is why priority-setting mods don't mix).
[/list]

[h1]Languages[/h1]
[list]
[*]Built-in support for English, French, German, Italian, Japanese, Korean, Brazilian Portuguese, Spanish (European and Latin American), Simplified Chinese, Traditional Chinese, Turkish, Ukrainian, and Vietnamese.
[*]No built-in Russian translation; community translation mods are welcome and override built-in text.
[/list]

[h1]Compatibility[/h1]
[list]
[*][b]Save Compatible:[/b] Safe to add to existing saves (priorities convert to roles) and safe to remove (the vanilla Work tab comes back sensibly populated).
[*][url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2606448745]RimWorld Multiplayer[/url] compatible.
[*]Requires [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2009463077]Harmony[/url].
[/list]

